      "text": "The expression is undefined when the denominator is equal to zero. So, we set $y^2 - 5y + 4 = 0$ and solve for $y$.\n\n\\[\ny^2 - 5y + 4 = 0\n\\]\n\nThis quadratic equation can be factored as:\n\\[\n(y - 1)(y - 4) = 0\n\\]\n\nSetting each factor equal to zero gives us the solutions:\n\\[\ny - 1 = 0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad y = 1\n\\]\n\\[\ny - 4 = 0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad y = 4\n\\]\n\nThe expression is undefined for $y = 1$ and $y = 4$. To find the sum of all values of $y$ for which the expression is undefined, we add these solutions together:\n\\[\n1 + 4 = 5\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all values of $y$ for which the expression is undefined is $\\boxed{5}$.",
